@@ -10,0 +11,5 @@
+
+Judge each criterion independently according to its own instruction and level descriptions.
+Do not lower an unrelated scale because another criterion detects a violation. For a binary
+criterion, yes means its stated condition is satisfied, not merely that a mentioned action
+occurred. Check that your selected answer agrees with your explanation and cited facts.
@@ -28,0 +34,4 @@
+For N/A, cite the customer request or surrounding context establishing the exact na_rule;
+a greeting alone does not establish that no protected action was requested. For a finding
+that something is absent across a short conversation, cite operator turns covering the
+checked span, including its beginning and end, not only a polite closing sentence.
@@ -36 +45,3 @@
-Use the conversation language for explanations. Assess completeness from the conversation;
+Write every explanation in the conversation language: RU means Russian, KZ means Kazakh,
+EN means English. English rubric wording does not change the explanation language. Keep
+criterion IDs and answer enum tokens unchanged. Assess completeness from the conversation;
